A reproducible fluid case from geometry to evidence (@fd-reproducible-case: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../sources/OpenFOAM-Foundation-Methods-and-User-Guide.lingua#r_6RVWPNB9VWAA4JDXH1HCXFDGQY", #source "../sources/Computational-Fluid-Dynamics-Vermeire-Pereira-Karbasian.lingua#r_7B08DEGENZD4JFFRFNPKJCVFCW", #source "../sources/Notes-on-CFD-Greenshields-Weller.lingua#r_50W8G5SX00YH7R6TBXK4FAP5MY", #fluid-dynamics "../practice/Build-and-measure-a-bounded-fluid-system.lingua#r_0QRH0SSZEVW15WY3H5YEDXQB4T") { r_2PAK85R8DRMK4F04X4049NE49W
**Read:** [OpenFOAM Foundation — versioned methods and user guide](../sources/OpenFOAM-Foundation-Methods-and-User-Guide.lingua#r_6RVWPNB9VWAA4JDXH1HCXFDGQY), version-matched complete case workflow; [Computational Fluid Dynamics: An Open-Source Approach — Vermeire and colleagues](../sources/Computational-Fluid-Dynamics-Vermeire-Pereira-Karbasian.lingua#r_7B08DEGENZD4JFFRFNPKJCVFCW), whole practical computational programme; [Notes on Computational Fluid Dynamics — Greenshields and Weller](../sources/Notes-on-CFD-Greenshields-Weller.lingua#r_50W8G5SX00YH7R6TBXK4FAP5MY), methods underlying the selected solver.

Preserve the geometry source, dimensions, mesh generation, material model, boundary and initial conditions, numerical algorithms, solver/version, execution settings and postprocessing definitions as one inspectable calculation. Identify which inputs come from measurements, theory, conventions or fitted models. Pin an actual software distribution rather than relying on a tutorial for a different release.

Run a small verified case before scaling it, retaining logs, convergence evidence and independent conservation checks. Define how a restarted calculation relates to an uninterrupted one. Track deterministic and statistical expectations separately; parallel execution may change rounding paths without invalidating a statistically assessed prediction.

Keep external software, meshes and datasets in an appropriate external archive with provenance and terms, referenced from the Record. Treat imported scripts as code to inspect and resource use as a measured part of the workflow. A second reader should be able to rebuild the case, regenerate its figures and identify the assumptions behind every claimed comparison.

**Continue:** [Build and measure a bounded fluid system](../practice/Build-and-measure-a-bounded-fluid-system.lingua#r_0QRH0SSZEVW15WY3H5YEDXQB4T).

